Axoniq Framework terms

  The Axoniq Framework modules and the Axon Server client are not open source. They are provided under the Axoniq
  Terms of Service, https://www.axoniq.io/legal/terms-of-service: free for development, demonstrations and CI, and
  a licence is required to run them in production. This repository uses them for development and CI only. The policy
  governance/dependency-licences.json lists each of them as an exception with its reason, and ./gradlew checkNotice
  fails when an exception is missing here.

  - `io.axoniq:axonserver-connector-java`: the gRPC client of Axon Server
  - `io.axoniq.framework:axon-server-connector`: the connection to the DCB-capable Axon Server
  - `io.axoniq.framework:axoniq-distributed-messaging`: command, event and query routing through Axon Server
  - `io.axoniq.framework:axoniq-framework-bom`: the bill of materials aligning the Axoniq Framework artifacts
  - `io.axoniq.framework:axoniq-testcontainer`: the Axon Server container of the integration tests (test scope)

Axon Server itself runs as a container image pinned in gradle/libs.versions.toml and is not part of this repository.
